      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please be very cautious about taking such a high dose of Vitamin C without consulting your doctor. While Vitamin C is good for you, excessive intake can sometimes increase the risk of oxalate stone formation in susceptible individuals. Instead, focus on a diet rich in fluids, potassium, and citrate-rich foods like citrus fruits and berries, and consider a low-oxalate diet if your doctor suggests it. Always discuss dietary changes and supplements with a healthcare professional to ensure they are safe for your specific condition.",
