      "content": "Sharp, stabbing pain and nausea are classic signs of kidney stone passage, but you should not self-treat with just ibuprofen and tea. These symptoms could indicate a serious blockage or infection that requires immediate medical attention. If the pain is severe, you need to seek prompt medical care to prevent kidney damage. Do not wait for it to resolve on its own; call your doctor or go to an urgent care center right away.",
